<spell-notebook "panel usage">
	<header level="1">
		Panel
		<header>A panel is an inspector:  a tinted box of fields under a header band, with sub-head bands that open and close.</>
	</>
	<panel-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#loading-a-band-from-a-file">Loading a band from a file</>
				<ui-item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  how to use it (attributes in practice, events, framework snippets), keyboard, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			A `<ui-panel>` is a [`<ui-section>`](/components/ui/ui-section.html) in an inspector's look, so it takes EVERY section
			attribute, slot, part and event: `label`, `hint`, `icon`, `badge`, `description`, `level`, `collapsible`,
			`open`, `fold-icon`, `sticky`, the `label`, `hint`, `icon`, `badge`, `actions` and `description`
			slots, `ui-opening` / `ui-closing` and `ui-opened` / `ui-closed`. Its vocabulary is built on the section's, so an attribute the section
			gains, the panel gains too.

			- Put fields straight inside: inputs, sliders, checkboxes, `<ui-field>`s. They stack 8px apart.
			- Nest a panel to start a sub-head band; its fields follow it.
			- `open` is controlled: set it to close or open; cancel `ui-opening` / `ui-closing` to keep the
			  user's click from changing it.
			- It needs no theme: under any theme it's a `primary`-tinted box. The brand pages' `spell-brand`
			  theme adds the `accent` hue (Polished Ivory) and the brand's shadow.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```js
			document.querySelector("ui-panel").addEventListener("ui-closing", (event) => {
			  if (unsavedChanges) event.preventDefault() // keep it open
			})
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Loading a band from a file">
		<markdown>
			`source` comes with `<ui-section source>` (being built in epic `claude-design`): a collapsed band
			loads its body from a file the first time it's opened. The panel takes it with no change of its
			own, as it takes every section attribute; until then the attribute does nothing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-panel label="Theme" collapsible>
			  <ui-panel label="Advanced" collapsible open="false" source="advanced.html"></ui-panel>
			</ui-panel>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<html>
			<ui-table celled padding="compact" unstackable>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Key</>
							<th>Action</>
						</>
					</>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Tab / Shift + Tab</>
							<td>Move to a band's open / close button, then its actions, then the fields</>
						</>
						<tr>
							<td>Enter / Space</>
							<td>Close or open the focused band</>
						</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- Each band is a real heading (`h2`, nested ones one level deeper), so panels appear in the page
			  outline.
			- A collapsible band's heading CONTAINS its open / close button, which says whether the content is shown
			  (`aria-expanded`) and which content it controls. The chevron is decoration.
			- Find-in-page reaches closed content and opens it.
			- Name every field: a panel's band doesn't label the controls under it.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
